## portus.application — la aplicación: rutas, middlewares, despacho y errores.
##
## Una `Application` guarda rutas (método + patrón + handler) ordenadas por
## especificidad, middlewares que corren antes y después de la ruta, y los
## hooks de error y ciclo de vida. El despacho construye un `Context` por
## petición y lo pasa siempre por `ref to`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var app as portus.Application is calling portus.new_application
## calling portus.get with sigil of app, "/", hello
## let served as result of int to string is calling portus.serve with sigil of app, 3000
## ```
##
## ## Memoria
## `free_application` libera las rutas, los middlewares y la arena de
## configuración. Los handlers y los hooks son código: no se copian.
import std.arena as arena_module
import std.scrolls
import portus.context as context_module
import portus.error as error_module
import portus.handler as handler_module
import portus.route as route
import portus.transport as transport

alias Context as context_module.Context
alias ErrorHandler as handler_module.ErrorHandler
alias Handler as handler_module.Handler
alias Middleware as handler_module.Middleware

## Hook de ciclo de vida (`on_start`, `on_shutdown`).
alias AppHook as weave with app as ref to Application into void

## Una ruta registrada.
rune RouteEntry:
    ## Método HTTP, o `"*"` para cualquiera.
    method as string
    ## Patrón compilado.
    pattern as route.Pattern
    ## Qué responde.
    handler as Handler
    ## Especificidad del patrón (mayor gana).
    score as int

## Un middleware registrado con el prefijo de rutas al que aplica.
rune MiddlewareEntry:
    ## Prefijo de ruta; `""` significa todas.
    prefix as string
    ## Qué ejecutar.
    middleware as Middleware

## La aplicación completa.
rune Application:
    ## Rutas ordenadas de más a menos específica.
    _routes as list of RouteEntry
    ## Middlewares que corren antes de la ruta, en orden de registro.
    _befores as list of MiddlewareEntry
    ## Middlewares que corren después de la ruta, en orden de registro.
    _finishers as list of MiddlewareEntry
    ## Arena para la configuración de los middlewares.
    _arena as arena_module.Arena
    ## Handler de error (por defecto, el de portus).
    _on_error as ErrorHandler
    _has_on_error as bool
    ## Handler de 404 (por defecto, el de portus).
    _on_not_found as Handler
    _has_on_not_found as bool
    ## Hooks de arranque y parada.
    _on_start as AppHook
    _has_on_start as bool
    _on_shutdown as AppHook
    _has_on_shutdown as bool
    # Una vez se presta la aplicación no se vuelve a copiar (modo debug).
    _sealed as bool

## Handler de error por defecto: deja que portus escriba la respuesta.
weave _no_error_handler with ctx as ref to Context, failure as HttpError into result of void to HttpError:
    return calling handler_module.err_void with failure

## Handler de 404 por defecto: no escribe nada; lo hace `respond_error`.
weave _no_not_found with ctx as ref to Context into result of void to HttpError:
    return calling handler_module.ok_void

## Hook vacío.
weave _no_hook with app as ref to Application into void:
    return

## Crea una aplicación vacía.
weave new_application into Application:
    var arena as arena_module.Arena is calling arena_module.Arena.new
    return with _routes is [], _befores is [], _finishers is [], _arena is arena, _on_error is _no_error_handler, _has_on_error is false, _on_not_found is _no_not_found, _has_on_not_found is false, _on_start is _no_hook, _has_on_start is false, _on_shutdown is _no_hook, _has_on_shutdown is false, _sealed is false

## Cuántas rutas hay registradas.
weave route_count with app as ref to Application into int:
    return app->_routes.len

## La arena donde viven las configuraciones de middleware.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un préstamo; la arena se libera con `free_application`.
weave arena_of with app as ref to Application into ref to arena_module.Arena:
    return sigil of app->_arena

## Registra un middleware que corre antes de las rutas en todo el árbol.
weave use with app as ref to Application, middleware as Middleware into void:
    calling app->_befores.push with (with prefix is "", middleware is middleware)

## Registra un middleware sólo para las rutas que empiezan por `prefix`.
weave use_at with app as ref to Application, prefix as string, middleware as Middleware into void:
    calling app->_befores.push with (with prefix is prefix, middleware is middleware)

## Registra un middleware que corre después de la ruta (para métricas, logs…).
weave after with app as ref to Application, middleware as Middleware into void:
    calling app->_finishers.push with (with prefix is "", middleware is middleware)

## Registra el handler que convierte un `HttpError` en respuesta.
weave on_error with app as ref to Application, handler as ErrorHandler into void:
    set app->_on_error is handler
    set app->_has_on_error is true

## Registra el handler de rutas no encontradas.
weave on_not_found with app as ref to Application, handler as Handler into void:
    set app->_on_not_found is handler
    set app->_has_on_not_found is true

## Registra un hook que corre al arrancar el servidor.
weave on_start with app as ref to Application, hook as AppHook into void:
    set app->_on_start is hook
    set app->_has_on_start is true

## Registra un hook que corre al detenerse el servidor.
weave on_shutdown with app as ref to Application, hook as AppHook into void:
    set app->_on_shutdown is hook
    set app->_has_on_shutdown is true

## Registra una ruta.
##
## `method` es `"GET"`, `"POST"`, … o `"*"`. El patrón se compila aquí; un
## patrón inválido es un error de programación y se devuelve como valor.
##
## ## Memoria
## La ruta guarda el `Pattern` compilado; el handler es código, no se copia.
weave add with app as ref to Application, method as string, pattern as string, handler as Handler into result of void to route.PatternError:
    var compiled as result of route.Pattern to route.PatternError is calling route.compile with pattern
    var pat as route.Pattern is compiled or:
        return calling err_of with error
    var entry as RouteEntry is with method is method, pattern is pat, handler is handler, score is pat.score
    calling app->_routes.push with entry
    calling _sort_last with app
    return calling ok_of with 0

## Reubica la última ruta en su sitio por especificidad.
weave _sort_last with app as ref to Application into void:
    var i as int is app->_routes.len - 1
    while i > 0:
        var previous as RouteEntry is (app->_routes at (i - 1))
        var current as RouteEntry is (app->_routes at i)
        if previous.score >= current.score:
            return
        set app->_routes at (i - 1) is current
        set app->_routes at i is previous
        set i is i - 1

## Libera las rutas, los middlewares y la arena. No libera el código.
weave free_application with app as ref to Application into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < app->_routes.len:
        var entry as RouteEntry is (app->_routes at i)
        calling route.free_pattern with entry.pattern
        set i is i + 1
    banish app->_routes
    banish app->_befores
    banish app->_finishers
    var arena as ref to arena_module.Arena is sigil of app->_arena
    calling arena.free

## Despacha una petición ya parseada: befores, ruta, finishers y error.
##
## ## Memoria
## Presta `request` y `response`; libera el `Params` que construye.
weave dispatch with app as ref to Application, request as ref to transport.Request, response as ref to transport.Response into void:
    var params as route.Params is calling _empty_params
    var ctx as Context is with request is request, response is response, params is params
    var failure as maybe HttpError is calling _run_befores with app, sigil of ctx
    if not failure.is_present and not calling response.is_sent:
        set failure is calling _run_route with app, sigil of ctx
    calling _run_finishers with app, sigil of ctx
    if failure.is_present and not calling ctx.is_sent:
        calling _handle_failure with app, sigil of ctx, (failure.value)
    calling route.free_params with ctx.params

## Un `Params` vacío (para peticiones que no encajan en ninguna ruta).
weave _empty_params into route.Params:
    return with names is [], values is []

## Corre los middlewares de antes. Devuelve el primer fallo, si lo hay.
weave _run_befores with app as ref to Application, ctx as ref to Context into maybe HttpError:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < app->_befores.len:
        var entry as MiddlewareEntry is (app->_befores at i)
        if calling _matches_prefix with ctx, entry.prefix:
            var outcome as result of void to HttpError is calling handler_module.invoke_middleware with entry.middleware, ctx
            if not outcome.is_ok:
                return some (outcome.error)
            if calling ctx.is_sent:
                return maybe none
        set i is i + 1
    return maybe none

## Corre los middlewares de después; sus fallos no cambian la respuesta.
weave _run_finishers with app as ref to Application, ctx as ref to Context into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < app->_finishers.len:
        var entry as MiddlewareEntry is (app->_finishers at i)
        if calling _matches_prefix with ctx, entry.prefix:
            var outcome as result of void to HttpError is calling handler_module.invoke_middleware with entry.middleware, ctx
            if not outcome.is_ok:
                return
        set i is i + 1

## ¿La ruta de la petición empieza por `prefix`?
weave _matches_prefix with ctx as ref to Context, prefix as string into bool:
    if prefix == "":
        return true
    return calling scrolls.starts_with with (calling ctx.path), prefix

## Busca la ruta y ejecuta su handler. Devuelve el fallo, si lo hay.
##
## Automatismos: `HEAD` cae en la ruta `GET` si no hay una `HEAD` propia (el
## transporte omite el cuerpo), y `OPTIONS` sin ruta propia responde `204` con
## `Allow`.
weave _run_route with app as ref to Application, ctx as ref to Context into maybe HttpError:
    var method as string is calling ctx.method
    var path as string is calling ctx.path
    var allowed as list of string is []
    var chosen as int is -1
    var chosen_params as route.Params is calling _empty_params
    var fallback as int is -1
    var i as int is 0
    while i < app->_routes.len:
        var entry as RouteEntry is (app->_routes at i)
        var found as maybe route.Params is calling route.match_pattern with entry.pattern, path
        if found.is_present:
            if entry.method == method or entry.method == "*":
                set chosen is i
                set chosen_params is found.value
                break
            if method == "HEAD" and entry.method == "GET" and fallback < 0:
                set fallback is i
                calling route.free_params with found.value
            else:
                calling route.free_params with found.value
                calling allowed.push with (calling route._copy with entry.method)
                if entry.method == "GET":
                    calling allowed.push with (calling route._copy with "HEAD")
        set i is i + 1
    if chosen < 0 and fallback >= 0:
        set chosen is fallback
        var fb as RouteEntry is (app->_routes at fallback)
        var again as maybe route.Params is calling route.match_pattern with fb.pattern, path
        set chosen_params is (again.value)
    if chosen < 0:
        if method == "OPTIONS" and allowed.len > 0:
            var options_allow as string is calling _join_methods with allowed
            calling route.free_strings with allowed
            var options_response as ref to transport.Response is ctx->response
            calling options_response.set_status with 204
            calling options_response.set_header with "Allow", options_allow
            calling options_response.mark_sent
            return maybe none
        if allowed.len > 0:
            var allow as string is calling _join_methods with allowed
            calling route.free_strings with allowed
            return some (calling error_module.method_not_allowed with allow)
        calling route.free_strings with allowed
        return some (calling error_module.not_found)
    calling route.free_strings with allowed
    set ctx->params is chosen_params
    var entry as RouteEntry is (app->_routes at chosen)
    var outcome as result of void to HttpError is calling entry.handler with ctx
    if outcome.is_ok:
        if not calling ctx.is_sent:
            return some (calling error_module.internal)
        return maybe none
    return some (outcome.error)

## Convierte un fallo en respuesta (o delega en `on_error` / `on_not_found`).
weave _handle_failure with app as ref to Application, ctx as ref to Context, failure as HttpError into void:
    var response as ref to transport.Response is ctx->response
    if failure.kind == HttpErrorKind.NotFound and app->_has_on_not_found:
        var not_found_outcome as result of void to HttpError is calling app->_on_not_found with ctx
        if not_found_outcome.is_ok and calling ctx.is_sent:
            return
        calling respond_error with response, failure
        return
    if app->_has_on_error:
        var outcome as result of void to HttpError is calling app->_on_error with ctx, failure
        if outcome.is_ok and calling ctx.is_sent:
            return
    calling respond_error with response, failure

## Junta métodos permitidos en el valor de `Allow`.
weave _join_methods with methods as list of string into string:
    var out as string is ""
    var i as int is 0
    while i < methods.len:
        if out == "":
            set out is calling route._copy with (methods at i)
        else:
            set out is "{out}, {(methods at i)}"
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Escribe la respuesta de error (a menos que ya se haya enviado algo).
##
## ## Memoria
## El cuerpo se copia en la respuesta.
weave respond_error with response as ref to transport.Response, failure as HttpError into void:
    var status as int is calling error_module.status_of with failure
    var message as string is calling error_module.message_of with failure
    calling response.set_status with status
    if failure.kind == error_module.HttpErrorKind.MethodNotAllowed:
        calling response.set_header with "Allow", message
        calling response.set_header with "Content-Type", "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
        calling response.write_text with "method not allowed"
        calling response.mark_sent
        return
    calling response.set_header with "Content-Type", "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
    calling response.write_text with message
    calling response.mark_sent

## Devuelve el puntero de la aplicación como `ref to void` sin tomar la dirección
## del parámetro (el código generado para una conversión implícita usaría `&app`).
antiquus _as_raw_context with app as ref to Application into ref to void:
    r"""
return (void *)app;
"""

## Arranca el servidor con la aplicación como despachador y unas opciones dadas.
##
## ## Memoria
## La aplicación debe vivir mientras el servidor corre (esta llamada bloquea).
weave serve_with with app as ref to Application, options as transport.ServeOptions into result of int to string:
    if app->_has_on_start:
        calling app->_on_start with app
    var outcome as result of int to string is calling transport.serve_loop_data with options, _serve_bridge, calling _as_raw_context with app
    if app->_has_on_shutdown:
        calling app->_on_shutdown with app
    return outcome

## Puente con `data`: reenvía al despachador de la aplicación.
weave _serve_bridge with data as ref to void, request as ref to transport.Request, response as ref to transport.Response into void:
    let app as ref to Application is transmute data to ref to Application
    calling dispatch with app, request, response
